<%# The bar an original in the archive wears: the way back to the archive, and
    nothing else. Held mail wears the pen's bar instead.

    It pointed at the reader until the reader was deleted. An original is
    reached from three places now — a story's citation, an archive row, and
    the pen — and only the pen has a back that differs, which it states in its
    own bar. The other two share the archive, so this stays one link rather
    than branching on where the reader came from. %>
<header class="topbar">
  <%= link_to t("newsletters.original.back"),
        newsletters_path,
        class: "topbar__back" %>
</header>
